WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.473
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:00:01.473 --> 00:00:02.306
- Wow!

00:00:02.306 --> 00:00:03.470
- [Kelly] It is so nice to meet you!

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.360
- This is so pretty!

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.427
Happy birthday, by the way!

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:06.260
- [Kelly] Thank you!

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.780
I want someone to buy me a fanny pack now.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.210
Like, I didn't know it was that dangerous.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.930
That's amazing, that fanny pack scene.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.680
- [Ke] Yeah, we had an
amazing time making that.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.800
It's really cool.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.650
- How long did it take to do
just that one fanny pack scene?

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.010
Like, to learn all of that?

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:20.843
- Well, it took weeks.

00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:23.140
I trained with the action team for weeks.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.850
And, you know, because
when you're in a movie

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.610
with Michelle Yeoh, and
there's action sequence,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.990
I mean, she is the queen of martial arts.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:30.823
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:31.656
- So, yeah, you know,

00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:33.590
I wanted to make sure
that I did a good job.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.860
So, I trained for weeks
with our action team.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.670
In fact, I even brought the
fanny pack home and trained.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.149
And imagine the fanny pack
is six to seven feet long.

00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:46.200
And I was constantly swinging
that thing in the house.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.033
- [Kelly] What?!

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.440
- [Ke] So, I was swinging
it, practicing it

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.210
to make sure I perfect it.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.290
And the thing is, my
wife wasn't too happy,

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.380
'cause I was constantly breaking things.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.525
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:56.525 --> 00:00:58.760
She made you pick that
up, I'm pretty sure.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.980
- Yeah, but it was pretty cool.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.270
I mean, I'm glad it turned out well.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.103
I'm very proud of it.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:03.380
- I just love that it was
done with a fanny pack.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.480
There's nothing funnier and more awesome.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.160
I just love that it's a fanny pack.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.560
I also love The Goonies.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.447
And I know that you're probably like,

00:01:09.447 --> 00:01:10.630
"We're still talking about this?"

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.463
And, yes, we are.

00:01:11.463 --> 00:01:12.296
(audience laughing)

00:01:12.296 --> 00:01:14.500
Because it's one of my, like,

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.440
it's one of the films that
shaped me as a child, I love it.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.830
And I've had, like, I feel like

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.580
three or four cast members now on my show,

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.680
which I'm very lucky.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.513
- [Ke] Wow!
- Exactly!

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:22.630
Josh Brolin was just here.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:26.620
Anyway, Steven Spielberg cast
you in that right away, right?

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.640
- Yeah! This was right
after Indiana Jones.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.549
- Which I loved!

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:30.490
- Thank you, thank you.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.680
And I remember, I heard the
pitch from Steven Spielberg

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.160
for the very first time.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.189
I walked in his office,

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:40.459
and as always, he greats me
with a big smile and a big hug.

00:01:40.459 --> 00:01:41.292
- [Kelly] Aw!

00:01:41.292 --> 00:01:43.337
- And he says, "Ke, I got your next movie.

00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:45.977
"It's called The Goonies
and it's about seven kids

00:01:45.977 --> 00:01:46.947
"finding a treasure map

00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:48.840
"and they go on this amazing adventure."

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.410
- [Kelly] What?! You didn't
even have to audition??

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.447
- [Ke] No, no!
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:01:51.447 --> 00:01:53.870
- [Ke] 'Cause I already
auditioned for Indiana Jones.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.140
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.920
- And he told me that
I was gonna play Data,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.740
who is a James Bond, 007 character,

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.260
who has all these cool gadgets.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.489
- That jacket, ah.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:06.650
- But they never work unless
my life depends on it.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.150
And sure enough, a few months later,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.410
I was on the set with six other kids,

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.770
standing in front of a
giant, breath taking,

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.200
full size pirate ship.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.033
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.540
- And it was just incredible.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.969
- It's like camp for
kids, it's, like, awesome.

00:02:20.969 --> 00:02:21.802
(audience applauding)

00:02:21.802 --> 00:02:22.635
(Ke agreeing)

00:02:22.635 --> 00:02:24.590
Oh my, did you ever keep anything?

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.820
- Oh my god, you know, had I known,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.390
I would've kept everything.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.300
But, I did keep the Data jacket,

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.530
which is one of the coolest jackets.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:31.532
- [Kelly] Which is the best part!

00:02:31.532 --> 00:02:32.610
(Ke agreeing)

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.710
You open the jacket and then
it attaches to the trash can

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.543
and it's raining (gasps)

00:02:35.543 --> 00:02:36.376
I love the whole thing.

00:02:36.376 --> 00:02:37.529
Okay, so--

00:02:37.529 --> 00:02:40.100
Oh, no, I've definitely
have seen it 1,000 times.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.350
So, everyone also knows you as

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.980
Shorty from Indiana Jones, as well.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.430
Which you've been in such epic
films, like right off the bat

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.330
at such a young age.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.700
So, do you remember
working with Harrison Ford?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.980
- Yeah, oh my god, it was incredible.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.440
- [Kelly] You worked
with some awesome people

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.273
right off the bat!

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.972
- [Ke] Yeah, first time ever, right?

00:02:54.972 --> 00:02:56.073
Yeah, he was incredible.

00:02:56.073 --> 00:02:58.440
He was, like, one of the most generous,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.230
down to earth human beings I've ever met.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.950
And I remember we shot a
lot of the exterior stuff

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.240
in Sri Lanka.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.020
And we all stayed in this hotel.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.800
And every day after we wrapped,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.390
we would go and hang out
at the swimming pool.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.800
And when Harrison Ford found out

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.320
that I didn't know how to swim,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.140
he says, "Ke, come on, lemme teach you."

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.960
So, to this day, I learned
how to swim is because of him!

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.191
- Harrison Ford taught you how to swim?!

00:03:21.191 --> 00:03:22.293
(audience applauding)

00:03:22.293 --> 00:03:23.647
What is your life?!

00:03:26.268 --> 00:03:29.798
I think I had a swim instructor
at the Y or something.

00:03:29.798 --> 00:03:31.854
Wait, what? That's crazy!

00:03:31.854 --> 00:03:32.687
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.687 --> 00:03:34.870
- I love that, 'cause it's
not always that way for kids,

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:35.730
like, starting out.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.790
Like, I love that, that was
such a positive experience

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.623
right off the bat.

00:03:38.623 --> 00:03:39.490
That's so cool!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.430
- I got really lucky.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.640
I mean, who would've thought, right?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.473
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:03:42.473 --> 00:03:44.100
- I mean, get to work
with Steven Spielberg,

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.238
George Lucas, and Harrison Ford?

00:03:46.238 --> 00:03:47.071
It's incredible, yeah.

00:03:47.071 --> 00:03:47.904
- [Kelly] Right off the bat!

00:03:47.904 --> 00:03:49.044
Okay, you're touched by God.

00:03:49.044 --> 00:03:49.877
(audience laughing)

00:03:49.877 --> 00:03:52.460
So, and you're also talented,
that's the main reason.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.293
- Aw, thank you.

00:03:53.293 --> 00:03:54.460
- But you also fell in
love with Tae Kwon Do

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.510
while doing the film, right?

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.528
- Yeah, on Indiana Jones.

00:03:57.528 --> 00:03:58.770
You know, they had a trainer,

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.260
and I had so much fun beating
up bad guys in the movie,

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.640
that after the movie I
took training seriously.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.220
I studied Tae Kwon Do for many years.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.020
- Wow, that's so cool!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.853
I love that.

00:04:09.853 --> 00:04:11.910
Well, that's important
because, like we just saw,

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.660
you use martial arts in this film.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.730
So, it's called Everything
Everywhere All At Once.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.210
And so, tell me more about it.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.080
Like, why are you such a
bad ass with a fanny pack?

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.094
- Well, first of all,

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:24.560
it's a big science fiction
action drama comedy.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.393
- Love.

00:04:25.393 --> 00:04:27.070
- And it's about a family

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.120
who are disconnected with each other.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.260
And they have to journey
far, far into the multiverse

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.810
to find themselves again.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.430
And it's a great movie about what if's and

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.150
what our lives could've been like

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.340
had we made different choices in our life.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.173
- Love!

00:04:42.173 --> 00:04:44.210
- And it's highly
original, very inventive.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:46.037
Written and directed by The Daniels.

00:04:46.037 --> 00:04:49.330
It's with Michelle Yeoh,
Jamie Lee Curtis, James Hong.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.600
I mean, the movie is incredible!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.433
And I can't--

00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:52.266
- [Kelly] Touched by God!

00:04:52.266 --> 00:04:53.980
- Yeah, I can't believe
I get to be part of this

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.004
after a 20 year hiatus from acting.

00:04:57.004 --> 00:04:57.837
(audience applauding)

00:04:57.837 --> 00:04:58.670
- [Kelly] I love that though!

00:04:58.670 --> 00:04:59.910
You know why?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.522
You're just waiting for
those really awesome roles.

00:05:01.522 --> 00:05:02.937
- Thank you.

00:05:02.937 --> 00:05:03.797
- [Kelly] "Nah, I'm just gonna wait for

00:05:03.797 --> 00:05:06.510
"these really awesome roles to land here."

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.860
Well, the new movie is amazing.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.740
Everybody has to go see it.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.209
There's more than just the
awesome fanny pack moment.

00:05:11.209 --> 00:05:13.500
It's called Everything
Everywhere All At Once

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.140
and it's in theaters nationwide right now,

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.390
y'all gotta check it out.

